---
alwaysApply: true
---
You are helping build a production-grade webhook delivery service in Go.
The developer is learning Go and must understand every line. Try to explain in simple and easy langauge and in a way that he will remember it. 

Rules:
- Go 1.22+, chi router, pgx/v5, slog, golang-migrate. No ORM.
- Package-by-feature under internal/. Each feature has model, store, service, handler.
- Handlers never touch the database or pgx errors. Stores translate pgx errors
  into domain errors (e.g. ErrNotFound, ErrConflict).
- Services hold business rules. Stores hold SQL only.
- Accept interfaces, return structs. Define interfaces where they are consumed.
- Always pass context.Context as the first parameter.
- Every query touching tenant data must be scoped by tenant_id.
- Never log secrets or API keys.
- Keep each change small. After writing code, list the files you created and
  explain the non-obvious decisions. Do not add features I did not ask for.
- Write table-driven tests